## 3. Acceptance gates

We will not mark an entire phase verified just because one command exits successfully.

| Gate | Evidence required |
| --- | --- |
| G0 — Inventory | File list, Git status and identified missing artifacts |
| G1 — Contract | YAML validation passes; all fields and UUIDs are unambiguous |
| G2 — Generation | Two runs produce identical output; generated files are current |
| G3 — Protocol | C and Kotlin agree with shared vectors; malformed inputs are rejected |
| G4 — Firmware | Clean build succeeds; no missing GATT or advertising implementation |
| G5 — Peripheral | Real board advertises and emits correct notification bytes |
| G6 — Android | App builds; permissions, connection and subscription work |
| G7 — State transition | Valid `MOTION_EVENT` changes `NORMAL` to `ELEVATED`; invalid packets do not |
| G8 — End-to-end | Repeated hardware-to-Android tests pass, with logs and results recorded |

